KEY DIAGNOSTIC LESSONS FROM THIS INCIDENT:
- Comparative traceroute across a single covering prefix (44.192.100.100 vs 44.192.0.100 within 44.192.0.0/16) surfaced the AWS internal loop that no single ping would have shown.
- The AltDB forgery attack pattern is real, cheap, and defended against structurally by the RIR-IRR-or-ROA-required filter policy — not by any single operator's vigilance.
- Asymmetric-source ping test (loopback vs unadvertised link IP as source) cleanly isolates return-path filtering from forward-path breakage when the forwarding decision is provably identical for both sources.
